    "body": "Breaking Defense’s Land Warfare Reporter Carley Welch speaks with Army Chief Technology Officer Alex Miller about the service’s autonomy plans, including the newly reflagged Futures and Autonomous Systems Command and its relationship to the Pentagon’s wider autonomy push .\nMiller highlights a drone marketplace that has handled more than $800 million in purchases and expanded beyond Army unmanned aircraft to include ground, maritime and counter-drone systems. Looking ahead, he says the Army sees autonomous tech supporting everything from battlefield protection to logistics, ammunition, food, fuel, water and medical supplies.\nSubscribe to our Pentagon newsletter to get the latest information from the building delivered directly to you.\nBreaking Defense Video\nArmy’s tech chief talks autonomy, acquisition and the future of drones\nWatch Now »\nDrones take over AUSA, plus the Army’s plan to bring in new vendors\nWatch Now »\nHegseth talks autonomy at AUSA, a key show focus\nWatch Now »\nArmy doubles down on autonomy, stakes out Indo-Pacific role: AUSA Day 2\nWatch Now »\nTelle talks ‘manufacturing rodeo,’ supply chain ‘weak links’: AUSA Day 1\nWatch Now »\nNew leaders, new drone command: What we expect from AUSA 2026\nWatch Now »\nUnpacking Boeing’s F/A-XX win, plus a report from wartime Ukraine\nWatch Now »\nHow Hegseth envisions a new Autonomous Warfare Command\nWatch Now »\nWhat Europe’s military air fleets will look like in 30 years\nWatch Now »\nRiyadh gets closer to F-35s, Damascus presses sovereignty and an expert take on Iran\nWatch Now »\nScroll for more video",
